 of an hour  they get along pretty well but then the  two are left alone without aoi yuto asks  sokake if he knows what things aoi likes  and dislikes her mannerisms her  ambitions in life or anything that a  partner should know sokake is guilty of  never paying much attention to his  girlfriend so he has nothing to say yuto  on the other hand lists the things that  aoi likes and explains how sokake can be  a better partner for her they eventually  get into a fight and yuto leaves for the  next few days he doesn't come to school  then one night aoi finds out sokake is  moving to tokyo to a better university  he will spend the next six years there  so the two will have to be in a  long-distance relationship to avoid  living apart he suggests that they move  in together however this will only be  possible if they get married it is a  trend for 16 year olds to get married  and start a family hence aoy gives it  some thought to clear her head she goes  to her uncles the next day he talks  about his chosen partner who moved  abroad when they were still together she  never returned and is happily married to  someone in london according to him  living with the penalties is easy if you  are with the person you actually love  although scared aoi feels ready to start  the new chapter of her life in the  following scene sokake and eoi are in  tokyo attending an open campus event aoy  is bored in the lecture but seeing  sokake enjoy it makes it worth it for  her after the lecture they visit several  places eat new food and have a lot of  fun in the end sokake brings her to a  church and gives her a little cat  compartment box that she had always  wanted it brings her joy which is then  multiplied when she finds an engagement  ring inside aoi says yes and the two  start preparing for the wedding she also  informs all her friends about the  proposal but a part of her still feels  empty because of yuto's absence  elsewhere yuto gets the wedding  invitation through the mail but doe